# Gradient of Anthropogenic Threat — website starter

A responsive static website based on the repository README and inspired by the GRooT reference layout.

## Files
- `index.html` — page structure and repository-derived content.
- `styles.css` — visual design, right-hand vertical navigation and responsive layout.
- `script.js` — mobile navigation and active-section highlighting.

## Run locally
Open `index.html` in a browser. No build step is required.

## Add real maps and figures later
The page currently contains clearly marked placeholders. Replace each placeholder `<div>` in `index.html` with an image, embedded map, or chart container when the final outputs are ready.

Suggested asset structure:
```text
assets/
  central-chile-landscape.jpg
  road-density-map.png
  loss-natural-ecosystems-map.png
  ghm-map.png
  gat-map.png
  biodiversity-diversity.png
  questionnaire-threats.png
  final-integration.png
  study-sites-map.png
```

For a simple image replacement, replace a placeholder block with:
```html
<img class="figure-image" src="assets/gat-map.png" alt="Gradient of Anthropogenic Threat map">
```
and add this CSS:
```css
.figure-image { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; object-fit:contain; }
```

## Before publishing
1. Replace the placeholder GitHub link in `index.html` with the actual repository URL.
2. Add real maps and plots to `assets/` when available.
3. Publish the folder with GitHub Pages (Settings → Pages → deploy from branch).

## Content note
Scientific descriptions and references follow the supplied repository README. No numerical results, map outputs, or empirical findings have been fabricated.

